        "prompt": "Find the value of $1-2+3-4+5-6$ by:",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p27-q7-a-i",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "i",
            "prompt": "working from left to right",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$-3$",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}1-2+3-4+5-6&=-1+3-4+5-6\\\\1-2+3-4+5-6&=2-4+5-6\\\\1-2+3-4+5-6&=-2+5-6\\\\1-2+3-4+5-6&=3-6\\\\1-2+3-4+5-6&=-3\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 47
          },
          {
            "id": "p27-q7-a-ii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "ii",
            "prompt": "pairing $(1-2)+(3-4)+(5-6)$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$-3$",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(1-2)+(3-4)+(5-6)&=(-1)+(-1)+(-1)\\\\(1-2)+(3-4)+(5-6)&=-3\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 24
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p27-q7-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Evaluate $1-2+3-4+5-6+7-8+\\ldots+99-100$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-50$\n\nThere are $50$ pairs, each with sum $-1$.",
          "worked": "Pair consecutive terms as in part a(ii). There are $100\\div2=50$ pairs, each with sum $-1$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}1-2+3-4+\\cdots+99-100&=(1-2)+(3-4)+\\cdots+(99-100)\\\\1-2+3-4+\\cdots+99-100&=50\\times(-1)\\\\1-2+3-4+\\cdots+99-100&=-50\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      }
